# Proposed specification (AGENT-PROPOSED, not student-approved)

Source: commit e500c44 + uncommitted working tree (see initial-source-status.txt).
No student-authored artifacts/specification.md exists; this is a fallback. It
carries forward run 20261102T235903Z-41864's proposed spec, updated for the
state of the tree (a build already exists from that run's 1-build attempt).

## Scope
- Port supplied doomgeneric (C) to WebAssembly with Emscripten 4.0.18.
  Browser target: current stable Chromium (Playwright).
- Only assets/doom1.wad, packaged with `--preload-file` at `/doom1.wad`,
  launched with `-iwad /doom1.wad`.
- Output dist/{index.html,doom.js,doom.wasm,doom.data}; served by
  `python3 -m http.server --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory dist`.
- Build: root `Makefile` (`make clean all`), documented in BUILD.md (not yet written).

## Functional requirements (proposed)
- R1 Boot: no console errors; title/menu appear.
- R2 Display: 640x400 `#canvas`; B,G,R,0 memory order converted to opaque RGBA.
- R3 Timing: ~35 tics/s real time; loop yields to the browser; wipe/tic waits do not freeze the tab.
- R4 Input: keyboard (arrows, Ctrl fire, Space use, Shift run, Alt strafe, Enter/Esc,
  digits, Tab automap, Y/N). Releases delivered; blur/visibility releases all keys.
- R5 Gameplay: New Game -> E1M1; move, shoot, use doors, state visibly changes.
- R6 Robustness: no crash/abort in a >= 5 minute scripted session.

## UNDECIDED (student decision needed; not claimed done)
- Audio (SFX/music), save/config persistence (IDBFS), mouse input,
  non-Chromium browsers, mobile/touch, hosting headers, and the definition of
  "faithful play" beyond R1-R6 (e.g. demo/determinism checks).
Faithful-play acceptance MUST NOT be reported complete while these are open.

## Assumptions
- emcc is not on the default PATH; a previous run found it by sourcing
  ~/Developer/emsdk/emsdk_env.sh. Version pin 4.0.18 must be confirmed with
  `emcc --version` at build time (not checked in this plan task).
- Single-threaded, ASYNCIFY build (no SharedArrayBuffer; no COOP/COEP needed).
- Fallback criteria live at tester/prepare/attempt-1/proposed-criteria.md in
  run 20261102T235903Z-41864 (tester-owned; this run has none). I did not
  create or edit criteria.
- Role isolation is instruction-only (manifest.txt); nothing here is enforced.
# Interface contract (AGENT-PROPOSED, not student-approved)

Authoritative declarations: `platform/capstone_bridge.h`, **version 2**.
Change from v1: added `cap_tic_count()` (already implemented in
platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c by the prior 1-build attempt, but the version had
not been bumped).

## Ownership
| File | Owner |
|---|---|
| platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c, platform/cap_fallback.c, platform/engine_stubs.c, platform/capstone_bridge.h, web/index.html, Makefile, BUILD.md | coder |
| platform/render_timing.{c,h}, web/render_timing.js | coder_render_timing (not yet delivered) |
| platform/input_audio.{c,h}, web/input_audio.js | coder_input_audio (not yet delivered) |
| tests/ | tester |

## Symbol table
| Symbol | Direction | Defined by | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| cap_bridge_version, cap_frame, cap_framebuffer_ptr, cap_tic_count, cap_ready | JS -> C (exported) | doomgeneric_wasm.c | cap_frame = one doomgeneric_Tick() |
| cap_render_init / cap_render_present(fb) / cap_time_ms / cap_sleep_ms / cap_set_title | C -> module | weak in cap_fallback.c; strong override in render_timing.c | present must not retain fb; time must be nonzero at first call |
| cap_input_init / cap_input_poll / cap_audio_init | C -> module | weak in cap_fallback.c; override in input_audio.c | poll returns 1 = event, 0 = empty |
| cap_input_event(pressed, doom_key), cap_input_reset() | JS -> C (exported) | weak in cap_fallback.c; override in input_audio.c | bounded queue; reset releases all keys |

## DG adapter mapping (doomgeneric_wasm.c)
DG_Init -> cap_render_init, cap_input_init, cap_audio_init; DG_DrawFrame ->
cap_render_present(DG_ScreenBuffer); DG_SleepMs -> cap_sleep_ms; DG_GetTicksMs
-> cap_time_ms; DG_GetKey -> cap_input_poll; DG_SetWindowTitle -> cap_set_title.

## Engine facts relied on
- DG_ScreenBuffer is 640x400 uint32 pixels, bytes B,G,R,0; alpha must be forced to 255.
- i_timer.c treats basetime==0 as unset, so DG_GetTicksMs must be nonzero on first call.
- Engine waits (d_main.c wipe loop, d_loop.c TryRunTics) call I_Sleep(1); real time
  must advance during them and the tab must not hang (current build: ASYNCIFY).
- Key codes are already Doom codes (doomkeys.h); I_GetEvent processes one release
  per call, so the queue must tolerate repeated polling.
- doomgeneric_Create() runs D_DoomMain and returns; main() calls it once and then
  drives doomgeneric_Tick() per frame.

## Weak/strong override rule
Specialist modules define the same symbols non-weak in their own platform/*.c;
the linker prefers them over cap_fallback.c. Makefile compiles platform/*.c.
Only the coder edits capstone_bridge.h; changes are requested via report.md and
require a CAP_BRIDGE_VERSION bump plus an update to this file.

## Build interface
`make clean all` -> dist/index.html, doom.js, doom.wasm, doom.data. Flags: -O2
-sASYNCIFY, --preload-file assets/doom1.wad@/doom1.wad (per prior build report).

## Open
Audio (`cap_audio_init` is a placeholder), persistence, mouse: UNDECIDED.
# Proposed acceptance criteria (AGENT-PROPOSED by tester; NOT student-approved) - revision 2, run 20261103T001738Z-47122

Basis: README.md, coder's proposed-spec.md (R1-R6) and interface-contract.md. No student
artifacts/acceptance-criteria.md existed. Student may replace/freeze these; until then they are provisional.
Implemented in `tests/playtest.mjs` (IDs match). Browser: Playwright Chromium 1.49.1 (131), viewport 800x600.

| ID | Criterion (observable) | Spec |
|---|---|---|
| B0 | `make clean && make all` succeeds from clean tree; dist/index.html + doom.wasm exist | build |
| B1 | `canvas#canvas` is 640x400 | R2 |
| B2 | Non-black frame with >16 colors within 60s of load | R1 |
| B3 | Canvas pixels opaque (alpha 255) | R2 |
| B4/B6 | Mean R >= mean B on title/menu and E1M1 (catches BGR swap) | R2 |
| B5 | No console errors, page errors, failed requests, or 404s | R1 |
| T1 | >=20 rAF/s over 3s (main loop yields) | R3 |
| M1 | Enter on title changes the display (menu opens) | R4/R5 |
| G1 | Enter x4 reaches a level: big change from menu and populated status bar | R5 |
| G2 | Idle frames stable (<2% pixels differ) | R5 |
| I1/I3 | Hold Right/Left turns the view: scene shifts >=8px in the correct direction | R4 |
| I2,I5,C3 | Motion/fire ceases after key release: I5 polls until settled (two consecutive 300ms steps <2%) within 4s, since Doom momentum decays ~1.5-2s | R4 |
| I4/I6 | Forward changes view and keeps changing while held; Backward returns closer to start | R4 |
| I7a/I7 | Holds ArrowRight (turn; wall-proof): I7a precondition view keeps changing; after blur the view settles within 4s and stays stable | R4 |
| T2 | `Module._cap_tic_count()` advances 35 tics/s +/-10% over 4s; missing export => UNVERIFIED | R3 |
| C1/C2 | Ctrl fire animates the view; ammo-counter region changes persistently | R5 |
| U1-U4 | Tab toggles automap and back; Esc opens/closes menu | R4 |
| R1-R4 | 300s scripted random-input soak: no errors/aborts, rAF >=20/s, last frame visible, frames changed, no longtask >=1.5s | R6 |
| selftest | Pixel helpers reject black / channel-swapped / transparent / static / mis-shifted frames | meta |

## Explicitly UNVERIFIED (reported every run; completion must not be claimed while open)
A1 audio (scope undecided; active AudioContext proves nothing), P1 save persistence, G3 door use /
level exit.
Also not covered: other browsers, mouse, touch, "faithful play" vs. original (e.g. demo/determinism checks).

## Known weaknesses of these checks
Pixel heuristics can false-fail on legit layout variation (e.g., canvas scaled with different aspect/letterbox,
HUD region assumptions) and can false-pass on identical-looking wrong gameplay. Backward-return check depends on
E1M1 geometry. Soak input is seeded pseudo-random; the player may die, so soak proves stability, not progress.

## Assumptions
Page serves from dist/ via any static server (test uses its own, no special headers); canvas has id `canvas`;
default menu path is Enter x4 with defaults; keyboard bindings are the Doom defaults in proposed-spec R4.
Change control: any later change to these criteria is recorded separately with a reason.

## Change log (rev 2, reason)
- I5/I6/I7: fixed settle delays replaced by polling (prior run's I5/I7 failures; coder measured momentum 1.2-1.5s). I7 now uses a turn key so walls cannot mask a stuck key.
- T2 moved from UNVERIFIED to checked now that cap_tic_count is exported (bridge v2).
